From 6c0d1ed5bd59f05deb02a2d73fac8314a75a4aee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:25:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] tourism: the venue pass on day 26, the attract step on
 the tick (B3 T2)

The month tick carried tourism's whole update. It is split in two:
- the venue pass (venues, historic sites, hotel rooms, beaches, hotels,
  the totals, the venue records and the visitor raster) runs in
  tourism.daily on TOURISM_DAY = 26, after that day's growables slice
  (tourismAcc v2: the window ends on day 26), and is saved as
  systemData.tourismPass v1 ([id, gross, op] records, [cx, cz, v]
  splats, culture, connections, college seats, kEff, beach / historic);
- the tick keeps the attract step (resident survey, attractiveness,
  migration, migrants), fed by the pass; a missing, invalid or stale
  pass (m !== ceil(day / 30)) is recomputed first.

The pass runs in ascending building id (venues, colleges, historic
sites): the runtime swap-removes from rt.plopped while a loaded game
rebuilds it in Map order, and the float sums and splats are not
order-free. init() restores a loaded city's records and raster exactly
from the pass; a city without one (new, or a save from before B3) takes
today's rebuild (refresh), keeping the saved totals unless the rebuild
feeds the coming tick (dom 26-29). onRemoved also takes a bulldozed
venue out of the coming tick's culture / connection scores (clamped at
0). The breakdown's culture / clean-air details stay with the tick that
scored them (tc, dump).

Behaviour changes by design (the bot's output changes): tourism totals
are 4 days older at the tick and reach demand and growth 4 days earlier.

Tests: tests/sim/monthSpread.test.ts (schedule, continuity of saves on
every day 31-60 with bulldozed and new venues, fallbacks, removal
between the pass and the tick, determinism, slicing); the tourism tests
use refresh(); the slices test is exact now. EM-1 normal play runs seed
3 over 6 years: seed 7's 4-year town raised 3 prompts before and 1
after (bot chaos; 5 seeds x 10 years: 21 vs 16 prompts).

